id: pm-vcs-00mb
title: Fail closed when repository configuration exists but cannot be read
description: "Discovered during served-repository adversarial testing: engine/config.ts readConfig catches every readFileSync error and returns DEFAULT_CONFIG. A repository whose .pmvcs/config.json has been replaced by a directory therefore advertises an empty record configuration rather than refusing. Distinguish absence from unreadable or invalid filesystem shape, preserve older repositories without a config file, and add FileTransport and HTTP parity tests. This is a pre-existing configuration-reader behavior; the HTTP feature records it as a separate follow-up."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-05T07:00:24.104Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T22:18:14.411Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-sol
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T19:28:39.394Z",codex-agent,"Plan: only ENOENT yields DEFAULT_CONFIG; wrap unreadable, JSON and schema failures in bad_config with the config path. Exercise real filesystem failures through FileTransport and HTTP, including legacy absent config."
  "2026-10-15T19:32:39.063Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only readConfig with origin/main makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"config failures refuse\" test/serve.test.ts fail (0 pass, 1 fail): directory config yields no exception. Fixed implementation passes and checks real directory, EACCES, malformed JSON, schema-invalid and ENOTDIR failures with bad_config and path; FileTransport and HTTP refuse; missing config works with a fresh server catalogue."
  "2026-10-15T19:35:10.945Z",codex-agent,"Linked pm test execution passed 1/1. Project test-result tracking is disabled, so the runner returned evidence_recording.recorded=false; recording the verified result here without changing project policy."
  "2026-10-15T20:02:33.122Z",codex-agent,"First full npm gate: 1540 passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped; every source file retained 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. The sole failure was an existing invalid-remote-root test expecting generic unreachable_remote for ENOTDIR. Updated that assertion to the requested typed bad_config with its config path; production behavior is unchanged from the fail-closed fix."
  "2026-10-15T20:20:21.589Z",codex-agent,"Expanded schema validation to reject explicit null recordPaths, recordPolicy and fields instead of silently using defaults; omitted fields still default. Config/FileTransport/HTTP parity and surrounding sync/catalogue tests pass 76/76. Additional behavioral revert proof: restoring only parseConfig from origin/main makes its malformed-shape regression fail with a missing expected exception; restoring the fix passes. Typecheck, lint and zero-duplication checks pass."
  "2026-10-15T21:04:35.522Z",codex-agent,"Complete npm release check at e03471b passed: 1541/1541 tests, 0 fail/cancel/skip/todo; all 65 source files retain 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. All subsequent acceptance, audit, pack, changelog and release-policy checks passed. The Bun-invoked run had one unrelated pre-existing erasure-setup refusal; an unchanged full retry is running."
  "2026-10-15T21:35:20.873Z",codex-agent,"Delivery gates at e03471b: npm run release:check and the unchanged full bun run release:check retry both exited 0, each with 1541/1541 tests and 0 fail/cancel/skip/todo. All 65 source files have 100% statements, branches, functions and lines (22526 statements/lines, 759 functions, 6563 branches). Thresholds and dependency pins are unchanged. Earlier unrelated erasure refusal is tracked in pm-vcs-simi. Final receipt changes only tracker evidence and the self-host bundle; release claim, keep in_progress."
  "2026-10-15T22:13:05.293Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: confirmed all three findings in PR #114. Distinguish a missing config entry from an unreadable dangling symlink using lstat before reading; retain deterministic directory refusal and probe chmod readability before running that subcase. Add real FileTransport and HTTP parity regression coverage and record behavioral revert proofs. Branch already contains origin/main."
  "2026-10-15T22:16:17.814Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof 1: with tests unchanged, replaced only readConfig with its pre-review HEAD implementation. node --test --test-name-pattern='config failures refuse FileTransport and HTTP: dangling-symlink$' test/serve.test.ts failed 0/1 (Missing expected exception). Restored the fix: all 9 config/legacy cases pass, including real symlink target removal. readConfig and FileTransport report bad_config; HTTP retains its intentional catalogue alias refusal with exact fixed denial status/body."
  "2026-10-15T22:16:23.777Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof 2: with tests unchanged, replaced only readConfig with origin/main's original read-error-to-default implementation. node --test --test-name-pattern='config failures refuse FileTransport and HTTP: directory$' test/serve.test.ts failed 0/1 (Missing expected exception). Restored the fix: directory refusal and chmod refusal pass through the reader, FileTransport and HTTP. The chmod test probes the real read result and explicitly skips with a reason when mode 000 remains readable; the deterministic directory fixture always runs."
  "2026-10-15T22:18:10.398Z",codex-agent,"Linked PM verification: 3/3 commands passed (8/8 config refusal cases, 1/1 invalid remote path, 1/1 legacy absence). Project test-result tracking is disabled, so outcomes are recorded here without changing that setting. Typecheck, lint and duplication checks passed; duplication remains 0% across 65 sources. Preparing the committed self-host snapshot before full gates."
